# --- OS cruft ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
ehthumbs.db
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# --- Editors / IDEs ---
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# --- Logs / temp ---
*.log
*.tmp
.cache/

# --- Local dev servers / tooling ---
node_modules/
# Playwright run output. The specs in tests/ ARE tracked; these are artefacts.
tests/__report/
tests/__results/
playwright-report/
test-results/
.netlify/
.vercel/
.wrangler/

# --- Env / secrets (don't commit credentials, API tokens, deploy keys) ---
.env
.env.*
*.local

# --- Owner-supplied source material, deliberately NOT tracked ---
# 14 MB of print PDFs, vector SVGs and 300/600dpi PNGs. The four files the site
# actually serves are committed in linen-works/. Re-supply from the owner if the
# assets ever need regenerating. See "Assets" in CLAUDE.md.
Logo/

# --- Personal, not project content ---
# Custom notification sounds for the local Claude Code hooks. Nothing on any of
# the three sites references them, and the hooks read their own copies from
# ~/.claude/sounds/, so the repo copy is only a convenient place to keep the
# masters. Ignored so a stray .mp3 can never be swept into a commit — or, worse,
# into a manual folder copy (Open work #10).
Sounds/

# --- Throwaway distribution builds ---
# Copies made for emailing a site out for review (JS inlined, unused assets
# stripped, because .js attachments are blocked). Rebuild rather than commit —
# see "Sending a site folder by email" in CLAUDE.md.
*-email.zip
*-email/

# NOTE: this is a plain HTML/CSS project with no build step, so there is no
# build-output folder to ignore. The .html, .jpg and .md files ARE the project
# and should all be committed. The Playwright harness (package.json, tests/,
# tools/, playwright.config.js) is DEV-ONLY — it never ships, and the sites
# still open straight from disk with no build.
